From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MeshGuard <noreply@meshguard.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] state: refuse auth sessions that are not node
 registrations

MeshGuard security patch 0001 (task P2-T10a, validation item V-26; root
cause, bypass analysis and tests: docs/planning/evidence/P2-T10a.md of
the MeshGuard repository). Not reported upstream: decision of the
project owner, 2026-11-17.

Node registrations and SSH check-mode sessions share the auth cache.
State.HandleNodeFromAuthPath fetched the cached entry and called
AuthRequest.RegistrationData without checking IsRegistration, so
RegisterNode/AuthRegister (CLI "headscale auth register", REST
POST /api/v1/auth/register) with the auth ID of a pending SSH check
panicked with "RegistrationData can only be used in registration
requests". The gRPC servers recover no panic, so the whole process
exited. The OIDC paths (oidc.go) and the registration follow-up
(auth.go) already check the kind of the session.

Refuse such an entry with state.ErrAuthRequestNotRegistration before
using it. RegisterNode returns it as codes.InvalidArgument, which the
REST gateway answers with HTTP 400 {"code":3,...}; the message does not
echo the auth ID. The session is left untouched, so its owner can still
approve or reject it. Registration entries take exactly the same path
as before.

Tests: hscontrol/grpcv1_auth_session_test.go (SSH check and verdict-only
sessions refused without panic and without side effect, the SSH check
still resolvable, a registration still registering, HTTP 400 through
the REST gateway).

Remove this patch when upstream checks the kind of the session in
HandleNodeFromAuthPath (or RegistrationData no longer panics), after
the MeshGuard contract test passes on that release without it.
